00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:24.390
That really just showing you

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.190
that the housing market
could be coming back,

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.200
and that'll be important
for the Federal Reserve.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.370
Last thing, we want to talk about

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.990
Business Conditions report.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:32.800
We get a number of reports out this week.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.020
We've already got

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.150
the U.S. Services and
Manufacturing reports.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.530
Those come out in Tuesday.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.990
Those are for May, and
that's the latest update

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.610
on business conditions in the U.S.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:42.600
You'll want to watch those,

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.760
because conditions have been deteriorating

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.170
through a lot of surveys.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.390
We get the Richmond Fed Survey on Tuesday.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.130
We get minutes from the Federal Reserve's

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.930
last policy meeting on Wednesday.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:52.950
That's going to tell us a lot,

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:54.450
and that could be market moving.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.940
We'll also get the Chicago
Fed National Activity Index

00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:00.090
on Thursday, the Kansas
City Fed Survey on Thursday,

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:03.900
and the Advanced Economic
Indicators report on Friday.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:04.920
That's going to tell us a lot

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.000
about the state of the economy,

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.190
and you'll want to watch that.
Listen that's going to do it

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.780
for us here on "Market Takes".

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.190
I'm your host, Dion Rabouin,

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.870
